    "_comment": "The Prism palette — the ONE source of UI colour (imported from the 'Prism UI Design Language': cold carved stone lit by sapphire rune-light, aged bronze the only structural metal, the 7-colour Septisigil for stats). Every colour elsewhere in this file is a `$name` reference resolved against this map. Stone ramp = surfaces (dark→light); edge = borders; ink/dim/faint = text; bronze = structural metal; sap_* = the interactive/live accent (base/hover/pressed + border + glow); rune_glow = lit text/focus; hp/mana/stam = resource ramps; sig_* = the seven stat colours. Derived translucent tokens (sheen/scrim/wash/panel_bg/hairline/cell_hot) are alpha variants of the same palette. stage_black = the one opaque black, the splash-letterbox plate behind baked-background logo images (TegLogo's plate is pure 0,0,0 — a stone backdrop would seam); status/state colours are NOT separate tokens: statuses speak Septisigil (sig_*) and the resource/danger ramps.",
